# Normalize line endings so Windows checkouts stay runnable inside Linux containers.
#
# Without this, a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true rewrites shell
# scripts to CRLF. The container then reads the shebang as `#!/bin/sh\r`,
# cannot find that interpreter, and the entrypoint dies with
# "exec: ./docker-entrypoint.sh: not found" — a message that looks like a
# missing file rather than a line-ending problem.

* text=auto

# Files executed inside containers MUST be LF, regardless of host platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
entrypoint*.sh  text eol=lf

# Keep container-bound config and robot description formats LF too.
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.urdf          text eol=lf
*.sdf           text eol=lf
*.xacro         text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts stay CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never touch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.wasm          binary

# ── Git LFS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Robot mesh assets and native binaries are large: the repo already carries 223 MB
# across 11 blobs, the biggest a 61 MB COLLADA trunk mesh that trips GitHub's 50 MB
# warning on every push.
#
# Scope is deliberately FORWARD-ONLY. The existing blobs live in main's history, and
# rewriting that would change every commit hash and stop this branch being a
# descendant of main. So these rules apply to newly added or modified files only;
# migrating what is already committed needs a coordinated
#   git lfs migrate import --include="*.dae,*.stl,*.node" --everything
# run against main, agreed with everyone holding a clone.
#
# NOTE: this supersedes the earlier `*.dae text eol=lf` rule, and is strictly better
# for it — LFS stores bytes verbatim, so the CRLF drift that had already corrupted
# four checked-out .dae files cannot happen to LFS-tracked meshes at all.
#
# Anything cloning or building from LFS-tracked assets needs `git lfs install`, and
# CI checkouts need `lfs: true`.
*.dae           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.stl           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.glb           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.node          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
